# One way round the loop is quiet, the other calls `weigh` and comes round too. A typed build over the list as it was tested in front of the head holds no call: it was left at the first part that has a size,
# and every later turn ran in the copy that is built for size. So such a loop is not bought a second build: there is one head, and the read of `size` is a guess in every turn.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-COUNT-1: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(SLOT): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# SLOT: isLoopHead=true
# SLOT: = GetSlot {{*}}key="size" receivers=[L0] level=Expected
# SLOT-NOT: = PropGet {{*}}key="size"
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 69
